## Two trees (scope)

| Tree | Role |
|------|------|
| `ooda/std/` | Product importable floor |
| `std/src/ooda/sec/crypto/` | Org sibling. **Not** the pure-path floor (`ooda/std/README.oot`) |

F31's original `find ooda` missed `std/`. That is why the audit said
"all 8 phantom." Wrong search root. Not all 8 are phantom. Five are.

---

## Name collision (F38b)

`ooda/std/core/crypto.oo` and `ooda/std/hash/sha256.oo` both declare
`fn sha256(String) -> String`. Bodies differ (CHS vs
`UNIMPLEMENTED_RESIDUAL`). Residual: which import wins.

---

## Known gaps (files that exist only)

None closed. None are products.

- **Falcon ops** — schoolbook `Int` mul; NTT/sign exit in stubs.
  Sampler / NTT not in this file.
- **secp256k1 ops** — no on-curve check; `is_valid` is length + flag.
  ECDSA/ECDH exit in stubs.
- **Plonk ops** — host `Int` field, not BN254. Pairing/FFT exit in stubs.
- **Ed25519 monofile** — clamp / point-mul / sign / verify exit.
  RFC 7748 clamp and on-curve not implemented.
- **Dilithium monofile** — public sign/verify **not** exited (D above).
- **Groth16 monofile** — pairing exits; structural verify is synthetic.
- **Double ratchet monofile** — KDF / DH / AEAD / send / recv exit.
- **Kyber** — only the `std/crypto/` facade exists; FO transform absent.
- **Constant-time** — no side-channel audit on any live body.

---

## What we do **not** claim

- No audited, production-grade crypto math.
- No 8-file load-bearing `process_exit` set.
- No constant-time guarantee.
- No Kyber at the listed `sec/crypto/kyber.oo` path.
- `"UNIMPLEMENTED_RESIDUAL"` is **not** `process_exit(1)`.

## Path A product floor (alpha)

- **In:** this restated ledger. Where `process_exit(1)` exists, the
  caller dies. Where the string residual exists, it is named.
- **Residual:** the math; string vs exit drift; CHS scope; synthetic
  verify; `sha256` name collision.

